  "authority_law": "RuleGraph never rolls dice, recomputes resolver output, writes campaign state, fabricates state facts, promotes source claims to canon, exposes secrets, or renders narration.",
  "model_integrity_law": "Candidate payloads must not contain sha256, digest, or hash fields. Digests are machine-computed at accept/build.",
  "coverage_law": "A shard may only assign accepted, partial, or absent to families it declared. Every other family is unresolved on the built graph. partial forbids runtime promotion. graph runtime ownership cannot coexist with a visible legacy Keeper surface.",
  "derivative_law": "Source-versus-derivative disagreement is recorded as a finding. The compiler never rewrites graph source claims to match a derivative.",
  "r1_promotion_law": "R1 never marks a family promotion-eligible. Absence of graph artifacts from a ruleset package defaults every family to legacy ownership with a visible legacy surface."
